{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If he comes alone, alone he shall go out.</b> According to its plain sense — as he came, so he leaves, as it explains and proceeds: if his master gives him a wife, a Canaanite maidservant, to bear children from her for his service, she and her children remain in the master's bondage, and he goes out as he came." "<b>Alone he shall go out.</b> Rashi explains: this teaches that if he was not married from the start, his master may not give him a Canaanite maidservant to bear slaves from her. For it does not come to teach that his master may give him a Canaanite maidservant but she does not go out with him, since that is derived from the wife and children. And the reason Rashi explained that if he was not married from the start his master may not give him a Canaanite maidservant is because there is reason to suspect lest he become attached to the Canaanite maidservant and come to say 'I love my master and my wife the maidservant,' and serve until the Jubilee. But when he is married from the start, he has longing for his Jewish wife and his Jewish children, and will not come to say 'I love my master and my wife the maidservant.'" "<b>And if he is married to a wife.</b> She is an Israelite woman at the time of the sale. <b>And his wife shall go out.</b> The Israelite woman, with him, in the seventh year. And since it said regarding the Canaanite woman that she remains, it was necessary to state regarding this one that she goes out with him. <b>And his wife shall go out with him.</b> To exclude a betrothed woman and a yevamah, who do not go out with him. Here Rashi explained that one who buys a Hebrew slave is obligated to provide food for his wife and children. And if you ask: from where do we learn that he is obligated to provide for their food? For it is written here only 'and his wife shall go out.' Rather, we derive it from another verse, in the section בהר: 'he shall go out from with you, he and his children with him.' And there 'his wife' is not written, and we learn here from there and there from here, to give what is stated of this one in that one and what is stated of that one in this one."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:14.795411441Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}